orted by the case evidence','Ignore Fisheries management and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Aquaculture as the only relevant consideration','Use Fishing gear technology without evaluating the information connected to Fisheries management','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',36),(2967,50,3,'A professional must choose between several reasonable approaches. The central issue is harvesting of fish and other aquatic resources from natural waters. Which decision best reflects sound analysis of Capture fisheries?','Ignore Capture fisheries and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fisheries ecology as the only relevant consideration','Select an approach grounded primarily in Capture fisheries and supported by the case evidence','Use Postharvest fisheries without evaluating the information connected to Capture fisheries','C','2026-10-08 05:33:10',37),(2968,50,3,'A team reviews an outcome that did not meet its intended goal. Because design and use of fishing gear for effective and responsible harvest, which interpretation of Fishing gear technology is most defensible?','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fishing gear technology and supported by the case evidence','Ignore Fishing gear technology and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fish nutrition as the only relevant consideration','Use Limnology without evaluating the information connected to Fishing gear technology','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',38),(2969,50,3,'A case includes incomplete information, multiple stakeholders, and potential consequences. Given that handling, preservation, processing, and quality control of aquatic products, which strategy best applies Postharvest fisheries?','Ignore Postharvest fisheries and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fish health as the only relevant consideration','Select an approach grounded primarily in Postharvest fisheries and supported by the case evidence','Use Oceanography without evaluating the information connected to Postharvest fisheries','C','2026-10-08 05:33:10',39),(2970,50,3,'A supervisor asks a student to justify a decision in a challenging case. Considering that study of inland waters and their biological and physical processes, which response shows the strongest reasoning using Limnology?','Select an approach grounded primarily in Limnology and supported by the case evidence','Ignore Limnology and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fisheries management as the only relevant consideration','Use Aquatic pollution without evaluating the information connected to Limnology','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',40),(2971,50,3,'A complex case involves competing priorities and limited time. The evidence indicates that study of marine environments and processes. Which approach best demonstrates higher-level application of Oceanography?','Ignore Oceanography and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Capture fisheries as the only relevant consideration','Select an approach grounded primarily in Oceanography and supported by the case evidence','Use Fisheries economics without evaluating the information connected to Oceanography','C','2026-10-08 05:33:10',41),(2972,50,3,'A professional must choose between several reasonable approaches. The central issue is effects and management of contaminants in aquatic ecosystems. Which decision best reflects sound analysis of Aquatic pollution?','Select an approach grounded primarily in Aquatic pollution and supported by the case evidence','Ignore Aquatic pollution and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fishing gear technology as the only relevant consideration','Use Fisheries law and policy without evaluating the information connected to Aquatic pollution','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',42),(2973,50,3,'A team reviews an outcome that did not meet its intended goal. Because economic analysis of fisheries, markets, and resource use, which interpretation of Fisheries economics is most defensible?','Ignore Fisheries economics and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Postharvest fisheries as the only relevant consideration','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fisheries economics and supported by the case evidence','Use Fisheries research methods without evaluating the information connected to Fisheries economics','C','2026-10-08 05:33:10',43),(2974,50,3,'A case includes incomplete information, multiple stakeholders, and potential consequences. Given that rules and governance systems for aquatic resources, which strategy best applies Fisheries law and policy?','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fisheries law and policy and supported by the case evidence','Ignore Fisheries law and policy and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Limnology as the only relevant consideration','Use Fish biology without evaluating the information connected to Fisheries law and policy','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',44),(2975,50,3,'A supervisor asks a student to justify a decision in a challenging case. Considering that scientific methods for studying aquatic resources and fisheries, which response shows the strongest reasoning using Fisheries research methods?','Ignore Fisheries research methods and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Oceanography as the only relevant consideration','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fisheries research methods and supported by the case evidence','Use Aquaculture without evaluating the information connected to Fisheries research methods','C','2026-10-08 05:33:10',45),(2976,50,3,'A complex case involves competing priorities and limited time. The evidence indicates that structure, function, growth, and life processes of fish. Which approach best demonstrates higher-level application of Fish biology?','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fish biology and supported by the case evidence','Ignore Fish biology and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Aquatic pollution as the only relevant consideration','Use Fisheries ecology without evaluating the information connected to Fish biology','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',46),(2977,50,3,'A professional must choose between several reasonable approaches. The central issue is controlled production of aquatic organisms. Which decision best reflects sound analysis of Aquaculture?','Ignore Aquaculture and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fisheries economics as the only relevant consideration','Select an approach grounded primarily in Aquaculture and supported by the case evidence','Use Fish nutrition without evaluating the information connected to Aquaculture','C','2026-10-08 05:33:10',47),(2978,50,3,'A team reviews an outcome that did not meet its intended goal. Because relationships among aquatic organisms, habitats, and environmental conditions, which interpretation of Fisheries ecology is most defensible?','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fisheries ecology and supported by the case evidence','Ignore Fisheries ecology and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fisheries law and policy as the only relevant consideration','Use Fish health without evaluating the information connected to Fisheries ecology','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',48),(2979,50,3,'A case includes incomplete information, multiple stakeholders, and potential consequences. Given that nutrient requirements and feeding of cultured and wild fish, which strategy best applies Fish nutrition?','Ignore Fish nutrition and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fisheries research methods as the only relevant consideration','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fish nutrition and supported by the case evidence','Use Fisheries management without evaluating the information connected to Fish nutrition','C','2026-10-08 05:33:10',49),(2980,50,3,'A supervisor asks a student to justify a decision in a challenging case. Considering that prevention, diagnosis, and management of disease in aquatic organisms, which response shows the strongest reasoning using Fish health?','Select an approach grounded primarily in Fish health and supported by the case evidence','Ignore Fish health and rely mainly on an unrelated routine','Treat Fish biology as the only relevant consideration','Use Capture fisheries without evaluating the information connected to Fish health','A','2026-10-08 05:33:10',50);
